; str-find-one-meaning-band.fk — ONE MEANING FOR THE SEARCH, HELD BY FOUR ARMS.
;
; str_find is what the tree scans with: split-on, find-from, trim's callers, every
; row walker and every key lookup reach a byte through it, at 1,596 call sites in
; form-stdlib alone. On 2026-09-08 the bearing census named `fstr-find-loop` at
; 35,147,894 calls and 64.3% of the locale walk with the remedy "mint-a-native",
; and the mint turned out to be a ROW: fkwu's tag-30 arm never left the C seed
; when the name left flt-ops on 2026-07-01, and neither did its fkc-tri2 arm in
; fkc-table-serialize.fk. Three of four mirrors were still standing. Restoring the
; row is what this band guards, and measuring its edges first is what found that
; the four kernels did not agree on what a search MEANS.
;
; WHAT DIVERGED, measured on this tree the same day, before the row came back:
;
;                                          fkwu     go / rust / ts
;   (str_find "abcdefghij" "" -3)          -3        0
;   (str_find "" "" -5)                    -5        0
;   (str_find "abc" "" -1)                 -1        0
;
; fkwu was the odd arm. A negative `from` is harmless for a non-empty needle — no
; byte matches below zero, so the scan walks up to the same answer — and for an
; EMPTY needle core.fk's recipe answered the negative number itself: a position
; that is not in the string. The three siblings had clamped since they were
; written. One arm out of four, in the guard's blind spot, for as long as both
; have existed.
;
; And a second one, quieter, in the other direction. go, rust and ts each snapped
; `from` UP to the nearest UTF-8 character start before searching, with a comment
; claiming a find-next loop would otherwise re-find a multi-byte match forever.
; It would not: +1 from a match lands on a continuation byte, where no well-formed
; needle can begin, so the scan advances on its own. What the snap actually did
; was skip real matches for a needle that IS a byte fragment — measured on the
; pre-heal Go kernel, `(str_find "aΩΩb" <the byte 0xA9> 2)` answered 4 where the
; byte answer is 2:
;
;                                          fkwu     go before    go after
;   [str_len, needle len, from 0, from 2, from 3]
;     "aΩΩb", needle = (substring "aΩΩb" 2 3)
;                                       [6,1,2,2,4]  [6,1,2,4,4]  [6,1,2,2,4]
;
; THE ONE MEANING, and it is this body's own — core.fk's `fstr-find` says it and
; fkwu's tag-30 arm has said it since before either of the wounds:
;
;   str_find(h, n, from) answers the BYTE INDEX of the first occurrence of n in h
;   at or after max(from, 0), or -1. An empty needle answers max(from, 0). A
;   max(from,0) past str_len(h) answers -1, the empty needle included. A needle
;   longer than what is left answers -1. Overlapping occurrences answer the first.
;   It refuses nothing and it FLOORS nothing.
;
; WHERE AN ARM CANNOT SAY IT. fkwu's strings are raw byte buffers and Go's string
; is an arbitrary byte sequence, so those two hold every needle. Rust's `str`
; carries a UTF-8 invariant and the TS kernel's string is UTF-16; neither can HOLD
; a needle that is a fragment of a multi-byte character, so `substring` hands them
; the axiom-1 absence there and str_find refuses out loud rather than answering.
; So the reading this band holds four ways is:
;
;   NO ARM EVER ANSWERS A DIFFERENT INDEX — the byte index, or the refusal.
;
; THE SNAP IS ASKED WITH THE EMPTY NEEDLE, and finding that question is most of
; what this band is. Stated the obvious way — "a needle beginning on a
; continuation byte is found at its byte index" — the property needs a needle
; rust and ts cannot hold, and the band's first form died there on `as_str: Null`
; while fkwu and go read 8191. But `str_find(s, "", i)` answers `i` itself, and
; the empty needle is representable on every arm, so an arm that snaps `from`
; answers a LARGER number at every byte inside a multi-byte character. The same
; wound, asked in a tongue all four speak — and stronger, because it holds at
; every byte rather than only at the bytes an arm can name. The absence
; discipline csfe-sweep-needles keeps stays beside it: the one-byte piece at a
; continuation byte is never a silent "" on any arm.
;
; THIS BAND IS THE GUARD, and ./validate.sh gates AGREEMENT, not correctness —
; three arms agreeing on a wrong index prints green, and for the negative `from`
; three of them agreed for months while the fourth did not. So this band pins the
; meaning itself: against a reference search it builds from str_byte_at on the arm
; under test, against literals the lexer carried into this source, and against
; every byte offset of the real multi-tongue rows off disk.
;
; Verdict 8191 (13 bits):
;   1     every `from` in [-4, 14] against six needles over a ten-byte ASCII
;         haystack equals the byte index this band's own scan finds — 114 cases
;   2     the clamping family named one by one: negative from, from at the length,
;         from one past it, from at a billion, empty needle at every position from
;         -2 to len+2, empty haystack, both empty
;   4     the answers pinned in this source as literals, not against bit 1's ruler:
;         the fifteen cases observe/line-grammar-pin-answers.fk prints
;   8     overlapping and repeated needles answer the FIRST occurrence, from every
;         start offset of "aaaaaa" and "abababab"
;   16    a needle at the very end, a needle equal to the whole haystack, a
;         one-byte needle, and a needle one byte longer than the haystack
;   32    multi-byte needles on character boundaries against source literals:
;         Greek, Persian, Hebrew, Chinese, Japanese and a four-byte emoji, each at
;         the byte offset the ruler gives — not a character offset
;   64    every character boundary of the multi-tongue literal: the character
;         standing there is found AT that byte offset, searching from it
;   128   the same, searching from the byte BEFORE it: a `from` inside a character
;         must not skip the match that starts at the next boundary
;   256   the real rows off disk, every character-start offset: the character
;         there is found at that offset, and a `from` past the end answers -1
;   512   the real rows off disk, every CONTINUATION byte: an empty needle
;         searched from there answers that byte offset itself — the property a
;         snapped `from` breaks, asked with the one needle every arm can hold —
;         and the one-byte piece there is never a silent ""
;   1024  the whole 972 kB corpus at full scale, held by natives alone — the
;         index returned IS an occurrence (cut it back out), nothing stands
;         before it, asking again from it is idempotent and asking past it moves
;         forward, an absent token answers -1 and a from past the end answers -1
;         — plus the ruler over a real 32 kB window of the same file
;   2048  the native and the body's own recipe agree: str_find equals fstr-find,
;         reachable by its own name in core.fk, over every case of bits 1 and 32
;   4096  the ruler is checked — this band's reference scan answers cases whose
;         answer is written in this source, so bit 1 is not a vacuous agreement
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOUR-WAY — 8191 live on fkwu, go, rust and ts (2026-09-08). The
; three walkers answer it through form/validate.sh; the fourth arm is fkwu's own
; resolver-driven source door, run every land as a drift gate row
; (gate/drift-gates.bml). It is NOT registered in fourth-arm-bands.txt: that
; manifest is the flatten lane, and we no longer flatten (Urs, 2026-08-27).
;
; WATCHED FAILING, on this tree, 2026-09-08. Three fkwu binaries were built with
; one deliberate wound each in the tag-30 arm and the band was run against them:
;
;   the negative clamp removed — fkwu's own meaning before this day
;                                       -> 6140   dark: 1, 2, 2048
;   `from` snapped up to a character start — go, rust and ts before this day
;                                       -> 7679   dark: 512, AND NOTHING ELSE
;   the `from > len` refusal dropped — the TS kernel's own wound, healed
;   2026-09-07, where str_find(h, "", 99) read 14
;                                       -> 5880   dark: 1, 2, 4, 256, 2048
;
; Bit 512 is the one that matters most and it behaved exactly as designed: the
; snap is invisible to every other bit in this band, and 7679 is the only number
; that separates a byte search from a snapped one.
;
; And against the PRE-HEAL BINARY — no tag-30 row at all, so `str_find` falls
; through to core.fk's recipe — this band reads 8191. That is not a miss; it is
; the point of keeping `fstr-find` reachable. The recipe and the native are one
; meaning, and the band cannot tell them apart. What the recipe cannot answer is
; a `nothing` from, where it walks up from nine quintillion below zero forever,
; and a non-string argument; neither is asked here, because neither has a
; four-way meaning.
;
; A guard nobody has watched fail is a guard nobody has checked.
;
; AND A GUARD NO ARM CAN AFFORD IS NOT A GUARD. The first form of bit 1024 held
; `str_find` against this band's own reference scan over the whole 972 kB corpus.
; That reference is a Form-level byte walk, and on the TypeScript arm one such
; pass had not finished after 12 minutes 46 seconds — the same cost, from the
; other side, that this whole heal is about. Full scale is now held by properties
; made of natives that a wrong search cannot satisfy together, and the reference
; walks a real 32 kB window of the same file. The band runs in seconds on all
; four arms, which is the only way it will actually be run.
;
; Expected: 8191
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    (defn sfm-bit (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))
    (defn sfm-and2 (a b) (if (and (eq a 1) (eq b 1)) 1 0))
    (defn sfm-and3 (a b c) (sfm-and2 a (sfm-and2 b c)))
    (defn sfm-and4 (a b c d) (sfm-and2 (sfm-and2 a b) (sfm-and2 c d)))
    (defn sfm-and5 (a b c d e) (sfm-and2 (sfm-and4 a b c d) e))
    (defn sfm-and6 (a b c d e f) (sfm-and2 (sfm-and4 a b c d) (sfm-and2 e f)))

    ; ── the ruler ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ; A byte scan built on the arm under test from str_byte_at alone — no
    ; substring, so it allocates nothing and re-encodes nothing (byte_to_str is
    ; not the exact dual above 127 on the three walkers; core.fk's byte-waist
    ; header carries that). It states the meaning: clamp the start, refuse past
    ; the end, an empty needle is at the start, otherwise the first position whose
    ; bytes all match.
    (defn sfm-eq-at (h n i j nl)
        (if (ge j nl) 1
            (if (eq (str_byte_at h (add i j)) (str_byte_at n j))
                (sfm-eq-at h n i (add j 1) nl)
                0)))
    (defn sfm-scan (h n i lim nl)
        (if (gt i lim) -1
            (if (eq (sfm-eq-at h n i 0 nl) 1) i
                (sfm-scan h n (add i 1) lim nl))))
    (defn sfm-ref (h n from)
        (do (let hl (str_len h))
            (let nl (str_len n))
            (let start (if (lt from 0) 0 from))
            (if (gt start hl) -1
                (if (eq nl 0) start
                    (sfm-scan h n start (sub hl nl) nl)))))

    (defn sfm-same? (h n from) (if (eq (str_find h n from) (sfm-ref h n from)) 1 0))
    (defn sfm-is? (h n from want) (if (eq (str_find h n from) want) 1 0))
    ; the recipe still reachable by its own name in core.fk
    (defn sfm-recipe? (h n from) (if (eq (str_find h n from) (fstr-find h n from)) 1 0))

    ; ── bit 1: every `from` against every needle ─────────────────────────────
    (defn sfm-sweep-from (h n f hi)
        (if (gt f hi) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-same? h n f) 1) (sfm-sweep-from h n (add f 1) hi) 0)))
    (defn sfm-sweep-needles (h ns lo hi)
        (if (eq (len ns) 0) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-sweep-from h (head ns) lo hi) 1)
                (sfm-sweep-needles h (tail ns) lo hi) 0)))
    (defn sfm-sweep-recipe (h ns lo hi)
        (if (eq (len ns) 0) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-recipe-from h (head ns) lo hi) 1)
                (sfm-sweep-recipe h (tail ns) lo hi) 0)))
    (defn sfm-recipe-from (h n f hi)
        (if (gt f hi) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-recipe? h n f) 1) (sfm-recipe-from h n (add f 1) hi) 0)))

    ; ── bit 2: the empty needle at every position around the ends ────────────
    (defn sfm-empty-at (h i hi)
        (if (gt i hi) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-same? h "" i) 1) (sfm-empty-at h (add i 1) hi) 0)))

    ; ── bit 8: the first of several ──────────────────────────────────────────
    (defn sfm-first-at (h n i hi)
        (if (gt i hi) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-same? h n i) 1) (sfm-first-at h n (add i 1) hi) 0)))

    ; ── the byte reading of a string, with no door but str_byte_at ───────────
    (defn sfm-cont? (s i)
        (do (let b (str_byte_at s i))
            (if (and (ge b 128) (lt b 192)) 1 0)))
    ; The byte offset where the character standing at a boundary i ends. THE
    ; LENGTH IS GUARDED BEFORE THE INDEX, and that is not a nicety: an
    ; out-of-bounds str_byte_at is ANSWERED by fkwu (-1) and is a deliberate fatal
    ; on go, rust and ts. The first form of this recipe asked for byte i+1 without
    ; checking it existed, read 8191 on fkwu, and killed the other three at
    ; index=43 len=43 on the last character of the multi-tongue literal. A band
    ; green on one arm and fatal on three is the shape running four ways exists to
    ; catch, and it caught this one before the door it guards was believed.
    (defn sfm-char-end (s i n)
        (if (ge (add i 1) n) n
            (if (eq (sfm-cont? s (add i 1)) 1) (sfm-char-end s (add i 1) n) (add i 1))))
    ; a one-byte piece is SOUND on this arm when it did not come back empty; on
    ; rust and ts a severed byte is the axiom-1 absence, which str_eq observes
    ; without dying and which is not str_eq to ""
    (defn sfm-sound? (s i) (if (str_eq (substring s i (add i 1)) "") 0 1))

    ; ── bits 64/128: every character boundary of a multi-tongue string ───────
    ; the character standing at i is found AT i, searching from i and from i-1.
    (defn sfm-bound-walk (s i n mode)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-cont? s i) 1) (sfm-bound-walk s (add i 1) n mode)
                (do (let piece (substring s i (sfm-char-end s i n)))
                    (let start (if (eq mode 1) i (if (le i 0) 0 (sub i 1))))
                    (if (eq (str_find s piece start) i)
                        (sfm-bound-walk s (add i 1) n mode) 0)))))

    ; ── bit 512: every continuation byte of a real row ──────────────────────
    ; THE BIT THAT SEPARATES A BYTE SEARCH FROM A SNAPPED ONE, and it is asked
    ; with the one needle every arm can hold. `str_find(s, "", i)` answers `i`
    ; itself — so if an arm snaps `from` up to the next character start, it
    ; answers a LARGER number at every byte inside a multi-byte character, and
    ; says nothing. That is the whole go/rust/ts wound, visible without ever
    ; asking for a needle rust and ts cannot represent.
    ;
    ; The first form of this bit asked instead for the one-byte FRAGMENT at i to
    ; be found at i, which is the same property stated with a needle only fkwu and
    ; go can hold: rust and ts died on `as_str: Null` before they could answer.
    ; The empty needle says it four ways. It is also stronger — it holds at every
    ; byte, not only at the bytes an arm can name.
    ;
    ; The absence discipline stays beside it: the one-byte piece at a continuation
    ; byte must never come back as a silent "" on any arm. Where it is a real byte
    ; (fkwu, go) it is a byte; where it cannot be (rust, ts) it is the axiom-1
    ; absence, which str_eq observes without dying — never a plausible empty.
    (defn sfm-cont-walk (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-cont? s i) 0) (sfm-cont-walk s (add i 1) n)
                (if (eq (sfm-sound? s i) 0) 0
                    (if (eq (str_find s "" i) i) (sfm-cont-walk s (add i 1) n) 0)))))

    ; ── bit 1024: full scale, held by natives alone ─────────────────────────
    ; None of these three can be satisfied by a search that is merely plausible,
    ; and together they need no reference walk: the answer is a REAL occurrence
    ; (cut the bytes back out and compare), nothing stands before it (search the
    ; prefix that ends where the answer begins), and asking again from the answer
    ; gives the answer back.
    (defn sfm-cut-back? (h n)
        (do (let i (str_find h n 0))
            (if (lt i 0) 0
                (if (str_eq (substring h i (add i (str_len n))) n) 1 0))))
    (defn sfm-first? (h n)
        (do (let i (str_find h n 0))
            (if (lt i 0) 0
                (if (eq (str_find (substring h 0 i) n 0) -1) 1 0))))
    (defn sfm-idempotent? (h n)
        (do (let i (str_find h n 0))
            (if (lt i 0) 0
                (if (eq (str_find h n i) i)
                    (if (gt (str_find h n (add i 1)) i) 1
                        (if (eq (str_find h n (add i 1)) -1) 1 0))
                    0))))

    ; ── bit 256: every character start of a real row ────────────────────────
    (defn sfm-rowstart-walk (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sfm-cont? s i) 1) (sfm-rowstart-walk s (add i 1) n)
                (do (let piece (substring s i (sfm-char-end s i n)))
                    (if (eq (str_find s piece i) i) (sfm-rowstart-walk s (add i 1) n) 0)))))

    (defn str-find-one-meaning-band ()
        (do
            (let h "abcdefghij")
            (let needles (list "a" "j" "cde" "abcdefghij" "zz" ""))
            ; a is 1 byte, Ω 2, each Persian and Hebrew letter 2, each Chinese and
            ; Japanese 3, the emoji 4 — the same literal substring-one-meaning-band
            ; measures at 43 bytes on all four arms
            (let mt "aΩ|گفت|שלום|中文|日本語|😀|z")
            (let mn (str_len mt))
            (let rows (read_file "form/form-stdlib/locale-rows/symbol-words.rows"))
            (let rn (str_len rows))
            (let corpus (read_file "learn/homecoming-distillation-corpus.fk"))
            (let cn (str_len corpus))

            (sum (list
                ; 1 — 6 needles x 19 starts against the ruler
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-sweep-needles h needles -4 14) 1) 1)

                ; 2 — the clamping family, one by one and by literal answer
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and6
                    (sfm-is? h "" (sub 0 3) 0)
                    (sfm-is? h "cd" (sub 0 3) 2)
                    (sfm-is? "" "" (sub 0 5) 0)
                    (sfm-is? h "" 10 10)
                    (sfm-is? h "" 11 -1)
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-is? h "a" 1000000000 -1)
                        (sfm-empty-at h (sub 0 2) 12))) 1) 2)

                ; 4 — the fifteen answers observe/line-grammar-pin-answers.fk prints,
                ;     as literals in this source
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and6
                    (sfm-and3
                        (sfm-is? "abcdefghijklmn" "" 99 -1)
                        (sfm-is? "abc" "" 0 0)
                        (sfm-is? "abc" "" 3 3))
                    (sfm-and3
                        (sfm-is? "abc" "" 4 -1)
                        (sfm-is? "" "abc" 0 -1)
                        (sfm-is? "" "" 0 0))
                    (sfm-and3
                        (sfm-is? "" "" 5 -1)
                        (sfm-is? "abc" "c" 0 2)
                        (sfm-is? "abc" "abcd" 0 -1))
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-is? "aaaa" "aa" 0 0)
                        (sfm-is? "aaaa" "aa" 1 1))
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-is? "said|گفت|sagte|dit|disse|spuse" "گفت" 0 5)
                        (sfm-is? "said|گفت|sagte|dit|disse|spuse" "|" 5 11))
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-is? "said|گفت|sagte|dit|disse|spuse" "spuse" 0 28)
                        (sfm-is? "said|گفت|sagte|dit|disse|spuse" "zzz" 0 -1))) 1) 4)

                ; 8 — overlapping and repeated: the FIRST, from every start
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and4
                    (sfm-first-at "aaaaaa" "aa" (sub 0 2) 8)
                    (sfm-first-at "abababab" "abab" (sub 0 2) 10)
                    (sfm-is? "aaaaaa" "aa" 0 0)
                    (sfm-is? "abababab" "abab" 1 2)) 1) 8)

                ; 16 — the ends and the whole
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and5
                    (sfm-is? h "j" 0 9)
                    (sfm-is? h "ij" 0 8)
                    (sfm-is? h h 0 0)
                    (sfm-is? h (str_concat h "x") 0 -1)
                    (sfm-is? h "a" 0 0)) 1) 16)

                ; 32 — multi-byte needles, at BYTE offsets, against source literals
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and6
                    (sfm-is? mt "Ω" 0 1)
                    (sfm-is? mt "گفت" 0 4)
                    (sfm-is? mt "שלום" 0 11)
                    (sfm-is? mt "中文" 0 20)
                    (sfm-is? mt "日本語" 0 27)
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-is? mt "😀" 0 37)
                        (sfm-is? mt "z" 0 42))) 1) 32)

                ; 64 — every character boundary of that literal, searching from it
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-bound-walk mt 0 mn 1) 1) 64)

                ; 128 — the same, searching from the byte BEFORE it
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-bound-walk mt 0 mn 0) 1) 128)

                ; 256 — the real rows off disk, every character start
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and3
                    (sfm-rowstart-walk rows 0 rn)
                    (sfm-is? rows "" rn rn)
                    (sfm-is? rows "" (add rn 1) -1)) 1) 256)

                ; 512 — the real rows off disk, every continuation byte
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-cont-walk rows 0 rn) 1) 512)

                ; 1024 — the whole 972 kB corpus, asked at full scale without the
                ;        ruler, and against the ruler over a real 32 kB window.
                ;        THE RULER IS NOT RUN OVER THE WHOLE FILE, and that is a
                ;        measured decision: it is a Form-level byte scan, and on
                ;        the TypeScript arm one such pass over 972 kB had not
                ;        finished after 12 minutes 46 seconds. A band no arm can
                ;        afford is not a guard. So at full scale the door is held
                ;        to properties made of natives that a wrong search cannot
                ;        satisfy together: the index it returns IS an occurrence
                ;        (cut it out and compare), it finds nothing before that
                ;        index, searching again from there is idempotent, and the
                ;        next search moves forward. The window keeps the ruler on
                ;        real bytes off disk at every position.
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and6
                    (sfm-cut-back? corpus "hdc-row 1354")
                    (sfm-first? corpus "hdc-row 1354")
                    (sfm-idempotent? corpus "hdc-row 1354")
                    (sfm-is? corpus "no-such-token-lives-in-this-corpus" 0 -1)
                    (sfm-is? corpus "hdc-row" (add cn 1) -1)
                    (sfm-and2
                        (sfm-same? (substring corpus 0 32768) "no-such-token-here" 0)
                        (sfm-same? (substring corpus 0 32768) "hdc-row" 0))) 1) 1024)

                ; 2048 — the native and the body's own recipe, by its own name
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and3
                    (sfm-sweep-recipe h needles -4 14)
                    (sfm-recipe? mt "گفت" 0)
                    (sfm-recipe? rows "|" 0)) 1) 2048)

                ; 4096 — the ruler answers what this source says it should
                (sfm-bit (eq (sfm-and6
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref h "cde" 0) 2) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref h "zz" 0) -1) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref h "" (sub 0 3)) 0) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref h "" 11) -1) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref "aaaa" "aa" 1) 1) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (sfm-ref mt "中文" 0) 20) 1 0)) 1) 4096)))))

    (str-find-one-meaning-band))
